Sure. You play lots of NetHack, you have to expect
that every 100 games, one _each_ of the "1% chance"
happenings are going to occur, and there's a *whole
lot* of those in NetHack, so most games you'll be
surprised by one or more of them.

0.72*0.72*0.72*0.72*0.72 is still almost a 20%
chance of failing five times in a row to write
Elbereth correctly. If you write Elbereth "a
lot", one time in five you should see your luck
be that bad. There's a reason Magicbane is so
popular.

The end of the lesson is that if you can, avoid
depending on luck _at all_. You can't, but make
that a goal of each move and see how many times
you can eliminate the RNG's chance to back-stab
you, because you found some cute trick to put
the RNG out of play.

